title: TUI renderer pi-tui, out-of-process mods, claude -p driver
summary: Founder chose pi-tui as the TUI renderer, out-of-process mods, and the claude -p stream-json driver for Claude sessions, and asked whether that uses API credits or the subscription.
symbols_touched:
  - '#paradigm-harness'
decisions:
  - id: P8-D32
    decision: 'TUI renderer: @earendil-works/pi-tui (MIT), with panes, virtualization and width-keyed line caches added'
    rationale: Small, framework-free, proven; deepseek-harness's long-session lesson addressed up front.
  - id: P8-D33
    decision: 'Mods run out of process: one child per mod over JSON-RPC, views from a closed kit, declared effects enforced at the boundary, approvals only from kernel-signed cards'
    rationale: No reference harness sandboxes mods; this keeps agent-written mods from touching the TUI or kernel.
  - id: P8-D34
    decision: Claude sessions driven by claude -p stream-json on the founder's subscription (add --include-partial-messages; plan mode and AskUserQuestion rendered as cards); preflight refuses if an API key would take precedence
    rationale: One pinned driver shared with flow and constellation.
